From b616176231dc1513e24c6e62547e3124fbd9a4d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 14:54:36 -0700
Subject: [RFC EXTENSIONS 3/3] RFC EXPERIMENT: net: flow_dissector: descend
 into VXLAN inner flow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THIS IS A BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, not a byte-identical fast-path. It is
posted for discussion alongside the VLAN / QinQ extensions, not as
something landable in its current form.

Today's flow_keys_dissector dissects to the *outer* of a VXLAN packet
(Eth + IPv4 + UDP, dst port 4789); the dissector has no UDP encap
descent for the standard dissector configuration. That means
overlay traffic between two VTEPs hashes onto a single 5-tuple
(outer src/dst + outer UDP src/dst + IPPROTO_UDP), which collapses
every inner flow into one bucket. Cake, fq, fq_codel, RPS, RFS, ECMP
— all of them see one flow.

This patch makes the dissector descend into the VXLAN payload when:

- The fast-path was entered (so the dispatcher gate is held).
- Outer is eth + IPv4 + UDP, dst port == IANA_VXLAN_UDP_PORT (4789).
- enough bytes remain for udphdr + vxlanhdr + ETH_HLEN.
- This is the first encap descent (encap_depth == 0; no nested-
  encap walk).

On match: set FLOW_DIS_ENCAPSULATION in key_control, advance nhoff
past udphdr + vxlanhdr + the inner Ethernet header, set proto from
the inner ethertype, and re-enter the dispatcher loop. The inner
ETH_P_IP / ETH_P_IPV6 fast-path overwrites key_basic / key_addrs /
key_ports / (and key_control->addr_type / thoff) with the inner
values — same shape as the slow-path encap descent in
__skb_flow_dissect_gre() etc.

What this gets you (operator-visible):

- Per-inner-flow hashing for VXLAN overlays in k8s. cake's
  per-flow fairness no longer collapses for east-west traffic
  between two VTEPs. RPS gets per-flow steering. ECMP between
  CNIs gets per-flow distribution.

What this breaks:

- Byte-identical with current behaviour. The contract of the
  parent fast-path series was "fast-path output == slow-path
  output." This patch knowingly violates that contract because
  the slow path doesn't have UDP-encap descent.
- Behaviour-on / behaviour-off symmetry. Today's
  net.core.flow_dissector_fastpath = 0 mode does not descend;
  today's = 1 mode (with this patch) does descend. That's an
  observable difference. The right shape for this work is
  probably:

    1) A separate sysctl, e.g.
       net.core.flow_dissector_descend_udp_encap, that gates
       the descent independently of the fast-path knob.
    2) Or a per-dissector flag (FLOW_DISSECTOR_F_DESCEND_VXLAN)
       that callers opt into.
    3) Or a UDP-encap descent in the slow path too, so the
       fast-path stays byte-identical.

- VXLAN port configurability. This patch hardcodes 4789. Real
  deployments often run on different ports (Cilium uses 8472
  for example). A landable version needs to consult the
  per-netns configured VXLAN ports.

- Nested encap (VXLAN-in-VXLAN, geneve-in-VXLAN) — guarded
  against here by encap_depth == 0 but not handled.

Posting this here primarily as a foothold to discuss whether the
flow_dissector's "stops at outer UDP" behaviour is the right
default. If consensus is no, this code shows what the descent
would look like; if yes, we have a clean record of the trade-off.

Signed-off-by: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
---
 net/core/flow_dissector.c | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/core/flow_dissector.c b/net/core/flow_dissector.c
index 044dc7c57406..83db01f9aba0 100644
--- a/net/core/flow_dissector.c
+++ b/net/core/flow_dissector.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <net/gre.h>
 #include <net/pptp.h>
 #include <net/tipc.h>
+#include <net/vxlan.h>
 #include <linux/igmp.h>
 #include <linux/icmp.h>
 #include <linux/sctp.h>
@@ -1215,6 +1216,7 @@ bool __skb_flow_dissect(const struct net *net,
 		enum flow_dissector_key_id vlan_key;
 		int thoff;
 		int vlan_depth = 0;
+		int encap_depth = 0;
 
 try_inner:
 		/* Up to two 802.1Q / 802.1ad tags (single VLAN + QinQ).
@@ -1334,6 +1336,50 @@ bool __skb_flow_dissect(const struct net *net,
 								      target_container);
 				key_ports->ports = *ports;
 			}
+
+			/* EXPERIMENT: descend into VXLAN inner for hashing.
+			 * This is *not* byte-identical with the existing slow
+			 * path — the standard flow_keys dissector stops at the
+			 * outer UDP today. Descending into the inner flow is a
+			 * behaviour change with operator-visible impact (k8s
+			 * overlays would get per-inner-flow fairness in cake
+			 * instead of per-VTEP-pair hashing). See the cover
+			 * letter; this commit is for discussion, not landable
+			 * as-is without wider review and likely an opt-in
+			 * flag.
+			 */
+			if (encap_depth == 0 &&
+			    iph->protocol == IPPROTO_UDP &&
+			    hlen - thoff >= (int)(sizeof(struct udphdr) +
+						  sizeof(struct vxlanhdr) +
+						  ETH_HLEN)) {
+				const __be16 *udp_ports = (const __be16 *)
+					((const u8 *)data + thoff);
+
+				if (udp_ports[1] == htons(IANA_VXLAN_UDP_PORT)) {
+					const struct ethhdr *inner_eth =
+						(const struct ethhdr *)
+						((const u8 *)data + thoff +
+						 sizeof(struct udphdr) +
+						 sizeof(struct vxlanhdr));
+
+					if (dissector_uses_key(flow_dissector,
+							       FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CONTROL)) {
+						key_control = skb_flow_dissector_target(flow_dissector,
+											FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_CONTROL,
+											target_container);
+						key_control->flags |= FLOW_DIS_ENCAPSULATION;
+					}
+
+					nhoff = thoff + sizeof(struct udphdr) +
+						sizeof(struct vxlanhdr) +
+						ETH_HLEN;
+					proto = inner_eth->h_proto;
+					vlan_depth = 0;
+					encap_depth++;
+					goto try_inner;
+				}
+			}
 			return true;
 		}
 
